msgstr "Which Anki scheduling states are included in the session pool.\n\n• New — cards you've never studied before\n• Learning — learning / relearning cards due now\n• Due / Review — mature cards scheduled for today\n\nNote: PDF, YouTube and Webpage cards are always eligible regardless of these checkboxes — they bypass Anki's scheduling state."
msgid "session_topics_ratio_help"
msgstr "Share of all session cards classified as Topics versus Items. Topics include document-reading cards.\n\nExample: 100 cards with 60% Topics / 40% Items targets 60 Topics (including documents) and 40 Items. Documents within Topics then divides only those 60 Topics.\n\n100% Items disables document Topics in normal mixing. Classification overrides and Advanced filters still apply."
msgid "session_document_mix_help"
msgstr "Percentage of Topics targeting PDF or EPUB document-reading cards. Items are unaffected.\n\nExample: 100 cards, 60% Topics / 40% Items, and 10% Documents within Topics targets 6 Documents + 54 other Topics + 40 Items.\n\n0% disables document Topics in normal mixing; 100% targets only documents within Topics. With 0% Topics this control is disabled, but its preference is remembered. Documents explicitly classified as Items remain Items.\n\nThis is a soft target, not an exact quota. Advanced content priorities may independently reserve documents before normal mixing."
msgid "session_selection_mode_help"
msgstr "How cards are selected from the eligible pool at each pick.\n\n• Priority (left) — picks the most overdue card first (sorted by due date). Use this to work through your backlog in order.\n• Random (right) — picks any eligible card at random. Use this for a varied, low-stakes session.\n\nExample: 99 % Random → almost always picks randomly; 1 % Priority → the most overdue card occasionally sneaks in."
msgid "session_scheduler_scope_help"
msgstr "How far back the scheduler looks when balancing card types and tags.\n\n• This session — debt resets each time you open this dialog. Best for: fresh start every day.\n• Today — debt accumulates across multiple same-day sessions. Best for: studying in several short bursts during the day.\n• All time — balances over your entire study history. Best for: strict long-term ratio enforcement.\n\nExample (Today scope, 90 % Topics target): if your morning session was all topics, the afternoon session will lean toward items to compensate."
msgid "session_priority_order_help"
msgstr "Use Order values to front-load each row's configured share before normal scheduling.\n\nExample: writing at 20% with Order = 1 means about the first 20% of the session will be writing cards. After that, the normal scheduler fills the remaining slots using your full mix. Empty or invalid Order boxes are ignored."
msgid "session_tag_quotas_help"
msgstr "Each slider sets the target share for this tag.\n\n• Soft mode (strict enforcement off): the % is a running target. The scheduler picks this tag more when it is under-represented and less when it is over-represented. Example: physics = 20 % → roughly 1 in 5 picks tries to find a physics card.\n\n• Strict mode (strict enforcement on): the Tags phase tries to fill a rounded number of places. Example: physics = 20 % with 50 cards → a target of 10 physics cards. Available cards and phase order can change the final mix.\n\nOther excludes all active selected tags and their subtags, even during refill. Cards with unrelated tags can still belong to Other.\n\nTag sliders with the same group name are constrained together to 100 %. Leave group empty to keep a tag independent. Total can exceed 100 % (a warning is shown)."
msgid "session_funnel_help"
msgstr "Only active when Strict enforcement is ON.\n\nStrict mode: each enabled phase fills its quota in full before the next phase starts. Drag phases to change the order; use ✓ to enable or disable individual phases.\n\nExample order: Content Types → Tag Quotas → Card Type → Selection Mode. First fill PDF / YouTube quotas, then tag quotas, then remaining slots using the topics / items ratio, then priority / random, and finally any ready card.\n\nSoft mode: the funnel is inactive. Phase order and the ✓ checkboxes have no effect. Instead, the scheduler blends all configured targets at every pick using a debt tracker, gradually converging on your ratios."
msgid "session_content_type_priorities_help"
msgstr "Reserve the first part of every session for a specific media type.\n\nThese cards are scheduled first (Phase 0), before Topics/Items ratios, Tag quotas, or Scheduling priority order take effect.\n\nExample: PDF = 30 % with 50 cards → the first 15 cards are always PDFs. After that, normal scheduling fills the remaining 35 slots.\n\nLeave unchecked for types you don't want to prioritise. If fewer cards are available than the quota, all available cards are used."
msgid "session_advanced_filters_help"
msgstr "Incremento classifies topics using the same logic as the T button, topic tags, configured topic note types, and the Topics deck.\n\nThese filters are optional extra narrowing on top of that classification. Leave them empty to use the full Incremento topic/item pools. Use 'Test' to check how many ready cards remain after narrowing."
